              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Incorrect. "
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "Solution"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " With Z = 92 and A = 122, U-214 is radioactive and will go through alpha decay. Stable isotopes have a ratio of neutrons to protons that locate the isotope within the band of stability shown on a plot of number of neutrons vs. number of protons for known nuclei. Unstable isotopes above the band have a ratio of neutrons to protons that is too high to be stable, and they will decay by beta decay to reduce this ratio. Unstable isotopes below the band have a ratio of neutrons to protons that is too low, and they will decay by alpha decay, positron emission, or electron capture to increase this ratio."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "njv0ifhbv3bf5zv",
                "type": "p"
              }
